cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use verified-ops-starter in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "verified-ops-starter: evidence instead of self-reports for scheduled jobs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/verified-ops-starter"
url: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/verified-ops-starter"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - observability
  - cron monitoring
  - AI agents
  - silent failure
  - fail-safe design
abstract: >-
  Three dependency-free checks that replace a job's self-report with evidence:
  freshness (is the real output young enough), wrap (did this run change anything),
  and rollout (is the fix on every box, read back as a fact). All three speak one
  exit-code contract in which a dead checker cannot look like a clean result, and
  every state in the test suite is produced by planting the actual failure first.
